<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20907" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hŏnōrus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		honor, analog. with decorus from decor (<b>poet.</b> and in postAug. prose). * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Worthy of honor</i>, <i>honorable</i>, <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 5,
			40</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>That confers honor</i>, <i>honorable</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carmen,</span>”
				<i>glorifying</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 4, 342</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fama,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 2, 629</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mors,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 230</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					1, 10 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae in Drusum patrem Germanici honora et
					magnifica Augustus fecisset,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">honora de Germanico disserebat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 68</span></i>
			.</div>
